<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Omer Bodson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1856">1856</a>–<a href="/years/1891">1891</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Omer Bodson (1856–1891) was a Belgian officer in the service of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congo-free-state">Congo Free State</a> and a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stairs-expedition-to-katanga">Stairs Expedition to Katanga</a>. At <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bunkeya">Bunkeya</a> on 20 December 1891 he shot dead the Yeke king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/msiri">Msiri</a> during a confrontation and was himself mortally wounded by Msiri's men. He was honoured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a> as a colonial hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/omer-bodson.jpg" alt="Omer Bodson" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Demetrius Charles de Kavanagh Boulger (1853-????) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Omer_Bodson,_Demetrius_C._Boulger%27s_Congo_State_(1898).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
